we just saw almost 20 minutes of ghost  of Tsushima gameplay and there's so much  to talk about here's everything you need  to know from the reveal the presentation  was split into four sections so we're  gonna do the same here  starting with exploration Tsushima  itself is a big island and developer  Sucker Punch wants it to guide you when  you open your map and place a waypoint  you won't get an intrusive GPS looking  line to guide you there instead small  gusts of wind will nudge the camera  toward the spot you marked on the way to  your destination you can pick up  resources like bamboo and you would  you'll also spot other points of  interest as you move along these include  smokestacks wild animals and what  sucker-punch describes as oddly shaped  trees you may also find shrines the demo  showed a fox actually guiding Jin to one  of these just like in the stories of  magical in re shrines you'll also be  able to fast travel between certain  destinations you've discovered like  Mongol camps that's where we'll get into  the next section combat combat is split  into two very different styles the  honorable samurai and the dishonorable  ghost samurai combat is fast and  dangerous with enemies slashing their  swords and firing arrows at you you can  change stances to deal with various  enemy types but combat is really all  about timing with the right timing you  can slice arrows out of the air or parry  an enemy's attack the ghost is all about  stealth however Jin can take out enemies  up close with a slice to the neck or  from a distance with his long bow or  kunai you can even take out a bunch at  once by lining up multiple instant  assassinations firecrackers serve as  great distractions and a smoke bomb can  disorient enemies and give you a chance  to escape the more you take out the  Mongols in these ways the more they will  fear you they may even drop their  weapons or run away customization is  also a big part of ghosts of Tsushima  but Jin's different armor isn't just for  looks yes you can make him look cool by  dying at different colors but different  armor types also offer combat advantages  omma more each arm also grant him  special perks and you can find them at  the aforementioned shrines the menu also  showed techniques you can learn an  upgrade letting you play as the samurai  or goes do you want to  speaking of seeing things we have to  talk about Tsushima special modes as you  might expect there is a photo mode with  various depth of field and color sliders  you can even use photo mode to record  video clips of yourself in action what's  more the game has what it calls samurais  cinema mode which paints the whole game  in black and white film grain in an  homage to the films of Akira Kurosawa  you can also experience the whole game  in full Japanese with subtitles right  from the start so yeah we learned quite  a lot about ghosts of Tsushima from that  stream and there's more to come before  it launches on ps4 on July 17th  in the meantime GameSpot has plenty more  coverage about all the features you  heard about here
 

